<title>POLAND: NBP DRAINS PLN 2.05 BLN FROM POLISH MONEY MARKET.</title>
<headline>NBP DRAINS PLN 2.05 BLN FROM POLISH MONEY MARKET.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland drained 2.05 billion zlotys from the market through a reverse NBP-bill repurchase auction after banks bid to place 2.05 billion with the central bank, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The bank drained 556.25 million zlotys for seven days at a maximum rate of 21.55 percent after banks bid to place 561.17 million with the central bank.</p>
<p>The bank drained 1490.93 for 14 days, the amount of bids, at a maximum rate of 21.65 percent, down from 21.70 percent on the last auction on December 20.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
